WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:09.930
Concern about the teaching critical race theory
in schools is percolating around the country,

00:00:09.930 --> 00:00:13.490
but at this point, a lot of Americans aren’t
familiar with the term.

00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:19.330
A June 2021 Morning Consult/Politico poll found
that 51 percent of registered voters had not

00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:21.880
seen, read, or heard anything about it.

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:27.020
A June Fox News poll found that 41 percent
of registered voters were not very or not

00:00:27.020 --> 00:00:31.280
at all familiar with it and another 8 percent
had never heard of it.

00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:36.620
Among those who knew about it in the Fox News poll,
37 percent said it should be taught in the public

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:39.430
schools, but 43 percent were opposed.

00:00:39.430 --> 00:00:45.010
In the Morning Consult poll, 32 percent said
it should be taught in K-12, with 36 percent

00:00:45.010 --> 00:00:46.120
opposed.

00:00:46.120 --> 00:00:48.750
Americans don’t want to sugar-coat US history.

00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:53.570
In a July Reuters/Ipsos poll, more than seven
in ten favored teaching high schools students

00:00:53.570 --> 00:00:57.660
about slavery and its impact, and separately,
about racism.

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:02.750
But many are clearly concerned that critical
race theory goes far beyond an even-handed

00:01:02.750 --> 00:01:06.316
portrayal of the country’s past and present.

00:01:06.316 --> 00:01:11.623
Should critical race theory be taught in schools? Let us know in our poll.

00:01:11.623 --> 00:01:15.941
Also, let us know what other topics you'd like our scholars to cover in 60 seconds,

00:01:15.941 --> 00:01:20.246
and be sure to like and subscribe for more research and videos from AEI.

